From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: report the Prospero SIGSYS origin

The Prospero SIGSYS route now reaches Wine's dispatcher, but Oblivion enters a
repeated STATUS_ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION loop from libSceLibcInternal. Log the
signal metadata and current Wine syscall frame before dispatch so we can tell
whether this SIGSYS came from a Windows syscall stub or from a native PS4
system call.

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -3263,6 +3263,13 @@ static void sigsys_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
     struct thread_data *data = init_handler( sigcontext );
     struct syscall_frame *frame = get_syscall_frame( data );
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    ERR_(seh)("Prospero SIGSYS code=%d errno=%d rax=%016lx rip=%016lx frame=%p frame_id=%08x frame_rip=%016lx\n",
+              siginfo ? siginfo->si_code : 0, siginfo ? siginfo->si_errno : 0,
+              (unsigned long)RAX_sig(sigcontext), (unsigned long)RIP_sig(sigcontext), frame,
+              frame ? frame->syscall_id : 0, frame ? (unsigned long)frame->rip : 0);
+#endif
+
     TRACE_(seh)("SIGSYS, rax %#lx, rip %#lx.\n", (long)RAX_sig(sigcontext), (long)RIP_sig(sigcontext));
 
 #ifdef __linux__
-- 
